{"name":"Slime","hex":"#a7c408","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"slime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Soft, moist earth or clay, having an adhesive quality; viscous mud; any substance of a dirty nature, that is moist, soft, and adhesive; bitumen; mud containing metallic ore, obtained in the preparatory dressing.","Any mucilaginous substance; or a mucus-like substance which exudes from the bodies of certain animals, such as snails or slugs."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To coat with slime.","To besmirch or disparage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slime coat","blocks":[{"text":"The slime coat is the coating of mucus covering the body of all fish. An important part of fish anatomy, it serves many functions, depending on species, ranging from locomotion, care and feeding of offspring, to resistance against diseases and parasites."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Eldon%27s_galaxias_%28Galaxias_eldoni%29_-_closeup_of_skin.jpg/330px-Eldon%27s_galaxias_%28Galaxias_eldoni%29_-_closeup_of_skin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slime_coat","wikidata":"Q118395950"},{"title":"Slime mold","blocks":[{"text":"Slime molds are a variety of small or microscopic organisms in different groups. They have both single-celled and multicellular forms during their life cycle, the individual cells coming together to form fruiting bodies that produce spores. Most live in damp places such as rotting wood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Comatricha_nigra_176600092.jpg/330px-Comatricha_nigra_176600092.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slime_mold","wikidata":"Q949817"},{"title":"Slime (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Slime, a German punk rock band founded in Hamburg in 1979, became a defining band in the 1980s German punk scene, and is the most widely recognized example of the musical style Deutschpunk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Slime_%E2%80%93_Hafen_Rock_2016_01.jpg/330px-Slime_%E2%80%93_Hafen_Rock_2016_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slime_(band)","wikidata":"Q238583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Hagfish_Slime_Predator_Deterrence.jpg/500px-Hagfish_Slime_Predator_Deterrence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Hagfish_Slime_Predator_Deterrence.jpg/500px-Hagfish_Slime_Predator_Deterrence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A seal shark (top, a–c) and an Atlantic wreckfish (bottom, d–f) each attempt to prey on a hagfish.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHagfish_Slime_Predator_Deterrence.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Lycogala_epidendrum_-_Pink_and_brown_slime_molds.jpg/500px-Lycogala_epidendrum_-_Pink_and_brown_slime_molds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Lycogala_epidendrum_-_Pink_and_brown_slime_molds.jpg/1280px-Lycogala_epidendrum_-_Pink_and_brown_slime_molds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Lycogala_epidendrum_-_Pink_and_brown_slime_molds.jpg/500px-Lycogala_epidendrum_-_Pink_and_brown_slime_molds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lycogala epidendrum was the first slime mold to be discussed scientifically, by Thomas Panckow in 1654.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALycogala_epidendrum_-_Pink_and_brown_slim